{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>There is one.</b> It is possible that 'two' means a companion or servant or a wife who is a helpmeet opposite him, and this is more correct." "<b>And there is no end to all his toil.</b> The matter is that he has wealth without end, yet his soul is not satisfied nor at rest from toil. Why does he not consider in his heart: for whom am I toiling? Why do I deprive my soul of every pleasure, when there is no one to inherit me, that my soul may rejoice to leave my son or my brother in good?" "<b>This too is vanity.</b> He added 'also' to indicate that the first fool is vanity like the last, and if both are fools — the wise one would be as the matter of 'poverty and riches do not give me' [cf. Proverbs 30:8]."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra alludes to Proverbs 30:8 ('רש ועושר אל תתן לי'); the Hebrew syntax is compressed and the citation is indirect."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:36.615532106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}